  "description": "CR 608.2c, 118.12a, 115.1, 701.6a: Repulsive Mutation puts X +1/+1 counters on target creature its controller controls, then counters up to one target spell unless that spell's controller pays mana equal to the greatest power among creatures the Mutation's controller controls",
  "note": "Alice controls Grizzly Bears (2/2) and Hill Giant (3/3); bob controls a Craw Wurm (6/4), which the greatest power ignores, and the target slot refuses. Turn 1 X=2 grows the Bears to 4/4, so the greatest is 4, not the Giant's 3 from before the counters: bob pays four and his Shock hits alice. Turn 3 X=4 grows the Giant to 7/7: bob declines and his Shock is countered. Turn 5 leaves the spell slot empty: the Bears get one counter, bob is asked nothing and his Shock hits alice.",
